nt-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-primary-dark transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Browse All Animals →\"}]]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐱\"}]\n46:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Fossa\"}]\n47:[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"desert-animal-names-arid-wildlife\",{\"href\":\"/blog/desert-animal-names-arid-wildlife/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🐪\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Wildlife Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Desert Animal Names: 120+ Arid Wildlife Ideas from the World's Driest Landscapes\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"120+ desert animal names from camels, fennec foxes, roadrunners, scorpions, and more. Hardy, resilient names for pets with desert spirit and survival instincts.\"}]]}]\n48:[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"the-ultimate-guide-to-playful-snowy-owl-names-175-ideas-for-every-snowy-owl-owner\",{\"href\":\"/blog/the-ultimate-guide-to-playful-snowy-owl-names-175-ideas-for-every-snowy-owl-owner/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🐾\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Snowy Owl Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"The Ultimate Guide to Playful Snowy Owl Names: 175+ Ideas for Every Snowy Owl Owner\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"From inspired by music inspirations to classic favorites, discover 175+ playful snowy owl names that capture your snowy owl's unique personality.\"}]]}]\n1a:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n17:null\n1c:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"From bearded dragons to dart frogs, discover 100+ creative names for reptiles and amphibians. Mythological, funny, cute, and fierce names for every cold-blooded companion.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.json\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"reptile names, amphibian names, lizard names, snake names, frog names\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"p:domain_verify\",\"content\":\"acc18c9aa2855ead49c874b6cac9cb61\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"6\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/reptile-amphibian-naming-guide/\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"From bearded dragons to dart frogs, discover 100+ creative names for reptiles and amphibians. Mythological, funny, cute, and fierce names for every cold-blooded companion.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"From bearded dragons to dart frogs, discover 100+ creative names for reptiles and amphibians. Mythological, funny, cute, and fierce names for every cold-blooded companion.\"}]]\n","/blog/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n9:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\"],\"\"]\n2c:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n2d:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n2:T2b33,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\",\"description\":\"From bearded dragons to dart frogs, discover 100+ creative names for reptiles and amphibians. Mythological, funny, cute, and fierce names for every cold-blooded companion.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-06\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/reptile-amphibian-naming-guide/\"},\"wordCount\":1473,\"articleBody\":\"📋 Table of Contents  Why Reptiles and Amphibians Deserve Thoughtful Names Reptiles and amphibians represent the fastest-growing segment of the exotic pet market, with bearded dragons, leopard geckos, corn snakes, and ball pythons becoming increasingly common in American households. The American Pet Products Association reports that approximately 4.5 million US households keep reptiles, while amphibian ownership continues to rise as captive-bred dart frogs, axolotls, and tree frogs become more widely available. Despite this growing popularity, dedicated naming resources for cold-blooded companions remain surprisingly scarce. Most pet name generators fail to capture the unique qualities that make reptiles and amphibians such fascinating and rewarding pets. Reptiles and amphibians deserve names that celebrate their ancient lineage, their otherworldly beauty, and the genuine personalities they develop under proper care. A bearded dragon who recognizes their owner and waves hello deserves a name as distinctive as any dog. A corn snake who explores their enclosure with methodical curiosity deserves recognition for their intelligence. An axolotl whose perpetual smile brightens every room deserves a name that matches their joyful presence. This guide provides 100+ names across multiple styles, each selected to honor the unique magic of cold-blooded companions. Mythological & Legendary Names for Reptiles and Amphibians Reptiles carry an undeniable connection to ancient mythology — dragons, serpents, and primordial creatures appear in virtually every culture's foundational stories. Naming your reptile or amphibian after mythological figures honors this deep ancestral connection while giving your pet a name of genuine weight and meaning. Draco, Latin for dragon, suits any lizard with impressive spines or an alert, intelligent gaze. Fafnir, the dwarf-turned-dragon from Norse mythology, carries ancient power perfect for bearded dragons or monitor lizards. Quetzalcoatl, the feathered serpent god of Aztec mythology, provides an exceptionally distinguished name for arboreal snakes or crested geckos. Additional mythological names: Jormungandr, the world serpent from Norse legend, suits large constrictors. Medusa channels Greek mythology for snakes with particularly striking patterns. Sobek, the Egyptian crocodile god, works wonderfully for aquatic turtles and crocodilians. Naga, serpent deities from Hindu and Buddhist traditions, provides gender-neutral elegance for any snake. Hydra, the multi-headed serpent of Greek myth, fits ambitious keepers who keep multiple reptiles. Amphibians draw from equally rich mythological traditions: Kappa, the water spirit of Japanese folklore, suits aquatic frogs. Tlaloc, the Aztec rain god, connects dart frogs to their rainforest origins. Funny & Punny Names for Reptiles and Amphibians The contrast between a \\\"scary\\\" reptile and a silly, lovable name creates instant warmth and memorability. Funny names also help counter the unfortunate stigma that snakes, lizards, and frogs are somehow less worthy of affection than furry pets. Sir Hiss offers classic snake humor with a touch of aristocratic dignity. Julius Squeezer combines historical reference with snake-appropriate wordplay. Snoop Frog channels music culture for amphibian owners with a sense of humor. Ribbit Downey Jr. provides celebrity-themed amphibian comedy at its finest. More punny names by species type: For lizards — Godzilla for tiny geckos (the irony makes it funnier), Liz Lemon for 30 Rock fans, Pascal for Tangled enthusiasts. For snakes — William Snakespeare, David Hisselhoff, Severus Snake (Harry Potter fans), Monty the Python (absolutely essential for python owners). For frogs — Frodo (for the tiny adventurer), Kermit (the classic that never gets old), Jeremiah (the bullfrog from the song), Hypnotoad for the Futurama faithful. For turtles — Sheldon (the obvious choice), Michelangelo for pizza-loving turtles, Franklin for the gentle, book-loving reptile. Each name brings humor while acknowledging the genuine affection owners feel for their scaled and shelled friends. Fierce & Powerful Names For reptiles with commanding presence — large monitors, impressive pythons, tokay geckos with attitude — names that convey power and intensity reflect their natural majesty. Titan suggests something ancient and unstoppable. Kaiser carries imperial German authority perfect for a confident, dominant reptile. Viper works across multiple species and carries undeniable edge. Fang celebrates one of the most defining features of snakes. Spikes suits iguanas and bearded dragons with impressive dorsal crests. Further fierce names: Rex (king), Khan (Mongol ruler), Thor (Norse thunder god), Ares (Greek god of war), Onyx (dark and impenetrable), Razor (sharp and dangerous), Diablo (for particularly spirited reptiles). Names like Venom and Shadow create an aura of mystery and danger, even for the most docile ball python who spends most days coiled peacefully in their hide. The contrast between fierce name and gentle animal creates exactly the kind of memorable personality that makes reptile keeping conversations so entertaining. These names acknowledge the wild ancestry within every captive reptile while celebrating their unique place in the animal kingdom. Cute & Tiny Names for Small Reptiles and Amphibians The smallest reptiles and amphibians — dart frogs no bigger than a thumbnail, baby leopard geckos that fit comfortably on a fingertip, newly morphed axolotls — deserve names that celebrate their diminutive charm. Pebble suits tiny frogs and geckos whose color patterns resemble polished stones. Bean describes the compact, round shape of certain frogs at rest. Pixel works for the digitally-small size of thumbnail dart frogs. Sprout captures the sense of new growth and tiny beginnings. Adorably tiny names: Pip, Dot, and Speck work for the very smallest creatures. Niblet and Nugget suggest something precious and bite-sized. Mochi describes the soft, squishy appearance of certain frogs. Jellybean captures the colorful, translucent quality of dart frogs and some gecko species. Button suggests something round and impossibly cute. These tiny names create a beautiful contrast with the ancient, evolutionary significance of these remarkable creatures — a dart frog carries millions of years of evolution and yet responds to Button with the same charm as any puppy named Spot. Naming Tips for Specific Reptile and Amphibian Species Different species have different naming considerations based on their natural history, appearance, and behavior. Bearded dragons are famously expressive and interactive, making human names like Bruce, Stella, or Gizmo particularly fitting. Leopard geckos with their permanent smiles suit cheerful names like Sunny or Joy. Ball pythons known for their gentle temperament deserve names that reflect their calm nature like Zen or Serenity. Crested geckos with their dramatic eyelashes inspire glamorous names like Lashes or Diva. For amphibians specifically: Axolotls with their perpetual smiles and external gills practically demand cute names like Puff, Gilly, or Smiley. Pacman frogs with their enormous mouths and sedentary lifestyle inspire food names like Pancake or Burger. Tree frogs with their sticky toes and climbing abilities suit acrobatic names like Sticky or Leap. Dart frogs with their brilliant warning coloration deserve gemstone names like Sapphire, Citrine, or Amethyst. The key is observation — spend time with your pet and let their unique behaviors and appearance guide your naming journey. For thousands more reptile and amphibian name ideas across hundreds of species, visit our complete animal name collection at bestanimalnames.com, where every name is curated and every generator is 100% free. Famous Reptiles & Amphibians in Pop Culture Popular culture has given us countless memorable reptiles and amphibians whose names make perfect pet inspiration. Godzilla needs no introduction — the King of Monsters provides an instantly recognizable name for large lizards, monitors, or any reptile with a commanding presence. Yoshi from Nintendo's Mario universe offers a friendlier, more approachable reptilian namesake perfect for gentle bearded dragons or friendly leopard geckos. Rango, the chameleon protagonist of the animated film, suits pets with quirky personalities and a flair for the dramatic. Explore our name generators for {antechinus}, {arapaima}, {archerfish}, {arabian-wolf}, and {arabian-leopard} to find the perfect name for your companion. From the amphibian world: Kermit the Frog remains the most iconic frog name in popular culture — instantly recognizable and perpetually charming. Michigan J. Frog, the top-hat-wearing, cane-twirling singing frog from Looney Tunes, provides one of the most delightfully specific frog names available. For snake owners, Nagini and the Basilisk from Harry Potter offer magical, serpentine naming options. These pop culture names connect your pet to shared cultural memories while providing excellent conversation starters for visitors meeting your reptile or amphibian for the first time. 🌍 A Real-World Naming Story Sometimes the best names come from the most unexpected places. Take Elena, a wildlife photographer who spent months observing rainbow-lorikeets in their natural habitat. When she finally adopted one as a pet, the name came naturally: 'Obsidian' — inspired by the volcanic rock formations where she first encountered the species. 'I didn't choose the name,' Elena recalls. 'The experience chose it for me.' This story illustrates a deeper naming principle: the most meaningful names aren't always found in lists or generators. They emerge from lived experience — a memorable trip, a childhood memory, a favorite artwork, a piece of music that moved you. These names carry stories, and stories are what transform a simple label into a lifelong connection with your animal companion. Discover more naming inspiration: {nile-monitor}, {yorkshire-terrier-dog}, {otter}, {king-cobra}, {banggai-cardinalfish}, and hundreds more animal name generators at BestAnimalNames.com.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-reptile-amphibian-naming-guide.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2\"}}],\"$L3\",\"$L4\",\"$L5\",\"$L6\"],null,\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"Vn-m7ZnH220y8-FGOgPuM\"}\n8:Ta6b,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do reptiles recognize their names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Reptiles can learn to associate specific sounds with positive experiences like feeding, though they do not recognize names the way dogs or parrots do. Consistent name use during handling and feeding can help your reptile associate the sound with positive interactions, making them more responsive over time.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are good names for a pet snake?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Good snake names range from mythological (Medusa, Nagini, Jormungandr) to funny (Sir Hiss, Julius Squeezer, Monty) to elegant (Onyx, Shadow, Luna). The best snake names reflect the snake's species, color pattern, and individual temperament. Ball pythons suit gentle names, while more active colubrids match energetic names.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I name my bearded dragon a funny name?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Absolutely. Bearded dragons have expressive, almost comical personalities that pair perfectly with funny names. Names like Pancake (for when they flatten out), Spike (for their beard), or Kevin/Todd (ordinary human names for an extraordinary lizard) bring humor while celebrating their unique charm.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the best names for pet frogs?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Popular frog names include Kermit, Frodo, Jeremiah, Hoppy, and Slippy. Species-specific names work well too: colorful names for dart frogs (Pixel, Jewel, Skittles), amphibious names for aquatic frogs (Splash, Paddles, Finn), and size-contrast names for tiny frogs (Goliath, Titan for a thumbnail-sized frog).\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I name my pet axolotl?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Axolotls with their pink gills and perpetual smiles inspire names like Gilly, Puff, Smiley, or Blush. Mythological water creature names also work beautifully: Ax (short for axolotl itself), Mudkip (Pokemon reference), or Toothless (How to Train Your Dragon). Their neotenic, forever-young appearance makes youthful, playful names especially fitting.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I name a reptile or amphibian I can't easily 'read' emotionally?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Focus on observable traits: movement patterns (slow = Zen, quick = Zip), coloration (vibrant = Jewel, Camo), feeding behavior (aggressive eater = Hunter, gentle = Grazer), and habitat preferences (burrower = Digger, climber = Summit). Physical traits become personality proxies for less expressive pets.\"}}]}3:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$8\"}}]\n4:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/reptile-amphibian-naming-guide/\\\"}]}\"}}]\n5:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500 flex gap-1 flex-wrap\",\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 font-medium\",\"children\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\"}]]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-6xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Reptile Names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"2026-06-06\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"By BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Reptile & Amphibian Naming Guide: 100+ Creative Names for Scales, Shells & Slime 🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"From bearded dragons to dart frogs, discover 100+ creative names for reptiles and amphibians. Mythological, funny, cute, and fierce names for every cold-blooded companion.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mt-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"reptile names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"reptile names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"amphibian names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"amphibian names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"lizard names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"lizard names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"snake names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"snake names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"frog names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"frog names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"📋 Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 to-indigo-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/10 mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\",\"children\":\"📋 Table of Contents\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 list-none pl-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[1,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#why\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Why Reptiles and Amphibians Deserve Thoughtful Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[2,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#mythological\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Mythological & Legendary Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[3,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#funny\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Funny & Punny Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#fierce\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Fierce & Powerful Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#cute\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Cute & Tiny Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[\"$La\",\"$Lb\"]}]]}]]}],\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\",\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\"]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L2c\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2d\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@2e\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#care\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Naming Tips for Specific Species\"}]\nc:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Why Reptiles and Amphibians Deserve Thoughtful Names\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Reptiles and amphibians represent the fastest-growing segment of the exotic pet market, with bearded dragons, leopard geckos, corn snakes, and ball pythons becoming increasingly common in American households. The American Pet Products Association reports that approximately 4.5 million US households keep reptiles, while amphibian ownership continues to rise as captive-bred dart frogs, axolotls, and tree frogs become more widely available. Despite this growing popularity, dedicated naming resources for cold-blooded companions remain surprisingly scarce. Most pet name generators fail to capture the unique qualities that make reptiles and amphibians such fascinating and rewarding pets.\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Reptiles and amphibians deserve names that celebrate their ancient lineage, their otherworldly beauty, and the genuine personalities they develop under proper care. A bearded dragon who recognizes their owner and waves hello deserves a name as distinctive as any dog. A corn snake who explores their enclosure with methodical curiosity deserves recognition for their intelligence. An axolotl whose perpetual smile brightens every room deserves a name that matches their joyful presence. This guide provides 100+ names across multiple styles, each selected to honor the unique magic of cold-blooded companions.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Mythological & Legendary Names for Reptiles and Amphibians\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Reptiles carry an undeniable connection to ancient mythology — dragons, serpents, and primordial creatures appear in virtually every culture's foundational stories. Naming your reptile or amphibian after mythological figures honors this deep ancestral connection while giving your pet a name of genuine weight and meaning. Draco, Latin for dragon, suits any lizard with impressive spines or an alert, intelligent gaze. Fafnir, the dwarf-turned-dragon from Norse mythology, carries ancient power perfect for bearded dragons or monitor lizards. Quetzalcoatl, the feathered serpent god of Aztec mythology, provides an exceptionally distinguished name for arboreal snakes or crested geckos.\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Additional mythological names: Jormungandr, the world serpent from Norse legend, suits large constrictors. Medusa channels Greek mythology for snakes with particularly striking patterns. Sobek, the Egyptian crocodile god, works wonderfully for aquatic turtles and crocodilians. Naga, serpent deities from Hindu and Buddhist traditions, provides gender-neutral elegance for any snake. Hydra, the multi-headed serpent of Greek myth, fits ambitious keepers who keep multiple reptiles. Amphibians draw from equally rich mythological traditions: Kappa, the water spirit of Japanese folklore, suits aquatic frogs. Tlaloc, the Aztec rain god, connects dart frogs to their rainforest origins.\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Funny & Punny Names for Reptiles and Amphibians\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The contrast between a \\\"scary\\\" reptile and a silly, lovable name creates instant warmth and memorability. Funny names also help counter the unfortunate stigma that snakes, lizards, and frogs are somehow less worthy of affection than furry pets. Sir Hiss offers classic snake humor with a touch of aristocratic dignity. Julius Squeezer combines historical reference with snake-appropriate wordplay. Snoop Frog channels music culture for amphibian owners with a sense of humor. Ribbit Downey Jr. provides celebrity-themed amphibian comedy at its finest.\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"More punny names by species type: For lizards — Godzilla for tiny geckos (the irony makes it funnier), Liz Lemon for 30 Rock fans, Pascal for Tangled enthusiasts. For snakes — William Snakespeare, David Hisselhoff, Severus Snake (Harry Potter fans), Monty the Python (absolutely essential for python owners). For frogs — Frodo (for the tiny adventurer), Kermit (the classic that never gets old), Jeremiah (the bullfrog from the song), Hypnotoad for the Futurama faithful. For turtles — Sheldon (the obvious choice), Michelangelo for pizza-loving turtles, Franklin for the gentle, book-loving reptile. Each name brings humor while acknowledging the genuine affection owners feel for their scaled and shelled friends.\"]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Fierce & Powerful Names\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For reptiles with commanding presence — large monitors, impressive pythons, tokay geckos with attitude — names that convey power and intensity reflect their natural majesty. Titan suggests something ancient and unstoppable. Kaiser carries imperial German authority perfect for a confident, dominant reptile. Viper works across multiple species and carries undeniable edge. Fang celebrates one of the most defining features of snakes. Spikes suits iguanas and bearded dragons with impressive dorsal crests.\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Further fierce names: Rex (king), Khan (Mongol ruler), Thor (Norse thunder god), Ares (Greek god of war), Onyx (dark and impenetrable), Razor (sharp and dangerous), Diablo (for particularly spirited reptiles). Names like Venom and Shadow create an aura of mystery and danger, even for the most docile ball python who spends most days coiled peacefully in their hide. The contrast between fierce name and gentle animal creates exactly the kind of memorable personality that makes reptile keeping conversations so entertaining. These names acknowledge the wild ancestry within every captive reptile while celebrating their unique place in the animal kingdom.\"]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Cute & Tiny Names for Small Reptiles and Amphibians\"]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The smallest reptiles and amphibians — dart frogs no bigger than a thumbnail, baby leopard geckos that fit comfortably on a fingertip, newly morphed axolotls — deserve names that celebrate their diminutive charm. Pebble suits tiny frogs and geckos whose color patterns resemble polished stones. Bean describes the compact, round shape of certain frogs at rest. Pixel works for the digitally-small size of thumbnail dart frogs. Sprout captures the sense of new growth and tiny beginnings.\"]}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Adorably tiny names: Pip, Dot, and Speck work for the very smallest creatures. Niblet and Nugget suggest something precious and bite-sized. Mochi describes the soft, squishy appearance of certain frogs. Jellybean captures the colorful, translucent quality of dart frogs and some gecko species. Button suggests something round and impossibly cute. These tiny names create a beautiful contrast with the ancient, evolutionary significance of these remarkable creatures — a dart frog carries millions of years of evolution and yet responds to Button with the same charm as any puppy named Spot.\"]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Naming Tips for Specific Reptile and Amphibian Species\"]}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Different species have different naming considerations based on their natural history, appearance, and behavior. Bearded dragons are famously expressive and interactive, making human names like Bruce, Stella, or Gizmo particularly fitting. Leopard geckos with their permanent smiles suit cheerful names like Sunny or Joy. Ball pythons known for their gentle temperament deserve names that reflect their calm nature like Zen or Serenity. Crested geckos with their dramatic eyelashes inspire glamorous names like Lashes or Diva.\"]}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For amphibians specifically: Axolotls with their perpetual smiles and external gills practically demand cute names like Puff, Gilly, or Smiley. Pacman frogs with their enormous mouths and sedentary lifestyle inspire food names like Pancake or Burger. Tree frogs with their sticky toes and climbing abilities suit acrobatic names like Sticky or Leap. Dart frogs with their brilliant warning coloration deserve gemstone names like Sapphire, Citrine, or Amethyst. The key is observation — spend time with your pet and let their unique behaviors and appearance guide your naming journey. For thousands more reptile and amphibian name ideas across hundreds of species, visit our complete animal name collection at bestanimalnames.com, where every name is curated and every generator is 100% free.\"]}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Famous Reptiles & Amphibians in Pop Culture\"]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Popular culture has given us countless memorable reptiles and amphibians whose names make perfect pet inspiration. Godzilla needs no introduction — the King of Monsters provides an instantly recognizable name for large lizards, monitors, or any reptile with a commanding presence. Yoshi from Nintendo's Mario universe offers a friendlier, more approachable reptilian namesake perfect for gentle bearded dragons or friendly leopard geckos. Rango, the chameleon protagonist of the animated film, suits pets with quirky personalities and a flair for the dramatic.\"]}]\n20:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/antechinus/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Antechinus\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"46\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arapaima/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arapaima\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"58\",{\"href\":\"/animal/archerfish/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Archerfish\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"72\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arabian-wolf/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arabian Wolf\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"92\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arabian-leopard/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arabian Leopard\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"p\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"From the amphibian world: Kermit the Frog remains the most iconic frog name in popular culture — instantly recognizable and perpetually charming. Michigan J. Frog, the top-hat-wearing, cane-twirling singing frog from Looney Tunes, provides one of the most delightfully specific frog names available. For snake owners, Nagini and the Basilisk from Harry Potter offer magical, serpentine naming options. These pop culture names connect your pet to shared cultural memories while providing excellent conversation starters for visitors meeting your reptile or amphibian for the first time.\"]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"24\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🌍 A Real-World Naming Story\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Sometimes the best names come from the most unexpected places. Take Elena, a wildlife photographer who spent months observing rainbow-lorikeets in their natural habitat. When she finally adopted one as a pet, the name came naturally: 'Obsidian' — inspired by the volcanic rock formations where she first encountered the species. 'I didn't choose the name,' Elena recalls. 'The experience chose it for me.'\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",\"26\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"This story illustrates a deeper naming principle: the most meaningful names aren't always found in lists or generators. They emerge from lived experience — a memorable trip, a childhood memory, a favorite artwork, a piece of music that moved you. These names carry stories, and stories are what transform a simple label into a lifelong connection with your animal companion.\"]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Discover more naming inspiration: \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"34\",{\"href\":\"/animal/nile-monitor/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Nile Monitor\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"50\",{\"href\":\"/animal/yorkshire-terrier-dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Yorkshire Terrier\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"75\",{\"href\":\"/animal/otter/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Otter\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"84\",{\"href\":\"/animal/king-cobra/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"King Cobra\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"98\",{\"href\":\"/animal/banggai-cardinalfish/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Banggai Cardinalfish\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and hundreds more animal name generators at BestAnimalNames.com.\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do reptiles recognize their names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Reptiles can learn to associate specific sounds with positive experiences like feeding, though they do not recognize names the way dogs or parrots do. Consistent name use during handling and feeding can help your reptile associate the sound with positive interactions, making them more responsive over time.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are good names for a pet snake?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Good snake names range from mythological (Medusa, Nagini, Jormungandr) to funny (Sir Hiss, Julius Squeezer, Monty) to elegant (Onyx, Shadow, Luna). The best snake names reflect the snake's species, color pattern, and individual temperament. Ball pythons suit gentle names, while more active colubrids match energetic names.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I name my bearded dragon a funny name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Bearded dragons have expressive, almost comical personalities that pair perfectly with funny names. Names like Pancake (for when they flatten out), Spike (for their beard), or Kevin/Todd (ordinary human names for an extraordinary lizard) bring humor while celebrating their unique charm.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the best names for pet frogs?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Popular frog names include Kermit, Frodo, Jeremiah, Hoppy, and Slippy. Species-specific names work well too: colorful names for dart frogs (Pixel, Jewel, Skittles), amphibious names for aquatic frogs (Splash, Paddles, Finn), and size-contrast names for tiny frogs (Goliath, Titan for a thumbnail-sized frog).\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I name my pet axolotl?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Axolotls with their pink gills and perpetual smiles inspire names like Gilly, Puff, Smiley, or Blush. Mythological water creature names also work beautifully: Ax (short for axolotl itself), Mudkip (Pokemon reference), or Toothless (How to Train Your Dragon). Their neotenic, forever-young appearance makes youthful, playful names especially fitting.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I name a reptile or amphibian I can't easily 'read' emotionally?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Focus on observable traits: movement patterns (slow = Zen, quick = Zip), coloration (vibrant = Jewel, Camo), feeding behavior (aggressive eater = Hunter, gentle = Grazer), and habitat preferences (burrower = Digger, climber = Summit). Physical traits become personality proxies for less expressive pets.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"bearded-dragon\",{\"href\":\"/animal/bearded-dragon/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦎\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Bearded Dragon\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"corn-snake\",{\"href\":\"/animal/corn-snake/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐍\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Corn Snake\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"ball-python\",{\"href\":\"/animal/ball-python/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐍\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Ball Python\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"leopard-gecko\",{\"href\":\"/animal/leopard-gecko/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$